    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") detection for owner creation. A new owner that isn't a *hard* duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone is still created, with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges, each kept in its natural home:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) fields to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them (and MapStruct maps them automatically by name).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the two persisted fields (`possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`) with getters/setters, mirroring the existing derived-at-creation fields (`namesakeCount`, `householdSize`). These persist so the value survives the `GET` re-read the test does.\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** and **`db/h2/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the two columns (the same two schemas that already carry `namesake_count`/`household_size`; postgres/mysql don't maintain those columns).\n\n4. **`PossibleDuplicateDetector.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility `@Component`, modeled on `NamesakeCounter`/`HouseholdMemberCounter`, that finds the matching existing owner (case-insensitive last name via `TextNormalizer`, equal postcode, different telephone), returning the lowest-id match or `null`.\n\n5. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 injects the detector and, for new owners (right beside where namesake/household counts are computed), stamps `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\nThe hard-duplicate rejection already runs in the controller before `saveOwner`, so this softer signal is only computed for owners that are actually going to be created. `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
